            "review_text": "Holms11\nTokyo, Japan520 contributions\n0\nBoutique Cafe with Good Decor\nOct 2018 • Family\nIt is on the 1st floor of Takashimaya and small but has good decor.\n\nI ordered Vietnamese coffee with fresh and condensed milk. When it was served, I was surprised. It was cafe latte! A cute heart mark was drawn on foamed milk! \n\nWhen I sipped, I was surprised again. It was so lukewarm! I felt it was about 30C. I remembered I had ordered “hot Vietnamese coffee\", but what I was served was “lukewarm cafe latte\"! Ummm...\n\nI ordered Black Forest Cake,too. It was not so good but not so bad. They were much more expensive than any other cafe in the city. It was not worth of trying.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 10, 2018",
